  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836984",
      "title": "Practice: Fetching Data",
      "sourceHash": "3a4dd9b72d4f09ee137310436375cbadcd15d6d9cf0956154379f924c36db528",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 4.32,
          "en": "Now fetching the places stored by the users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.32,
          "end": 6.99,
          "en": "works pretty much exactly as it did",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.99,
          "end": 9.813,
          "en": "for fetching the available places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.86,
          "end": 14.22,
          "en": "We wanna do that right away when the app component renders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.22,
          "end": 15.69,
          "en": "for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.69,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "And, of course, therefore, to avoid an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 21.03,
          "en": "when we then update the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.03,
          "end": 23.793,
          "en": "we should do that with help of useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.59,
          "end": 27.72,
          "en": "Therefore, to fetch those places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 31.17,
          "en": "I'll start by going to HTTP JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.17,
          "end": 33.09,
          "en": "And there we can start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.09,
          "end": 37.413,
          "en": "by copying the fetchAvailablePlaces function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 41.85,
          "en": "And I'll now rename that copy to fetchUsrPlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.5,
          "end": 45.81,
          "en": "because the logic is almost the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.81,
          "end": 49.44,
          "en": "but we should send the request to user-places here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.44,
          "end": 54.18,
          "en": "at the end and we might want to tweak the error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.18,
          "end": 57.243,
          "en": "to failed to fetch user places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.14,
          "end": 61.87,
          "en": "But other than that, this function can stay the way it is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 65.973,
          "en": "and we can go back to the app JSX file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.26,
          "end": 71.245,
          "en": "And in here, as mentioned, we should now fetch those places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.245,
          "end": 73.257,
          "en": "with help of useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.19200000000001,
          "end": 77.667,
          "en": "So that should be imported from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.63,
          "end": 85.17,
          "en": "and with it imported, we define the effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 85.17,
          "end": 87.363,
          "en": "and this dependencies array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.26,
          "end": 92.07,
          "en": "And in the effect function we can add an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.07,
          "end": 96.15,
          "en": "called \"fetchPlaces\" so that we can use async await",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 96.15,
          "end": 100.14,
          "en": "and we should then also execute this function right away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 100.14,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "just as we did it before in available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 107.253,
          "en": "where we also defined such a helper function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 114.12,
          "en": "Now here in App JSX, in that fetchPlaces helper function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.12,
          "end": 117.887,
          "en": "we can now await calling fetchUserPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 119.52000000000001,
          "end": 122.64,
          "en": "So this function we just copied and edited inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 122.64,
          "end": 126.393,
          "en": "of HTTP JS, which therefore also must be imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 133.47,
          "en": "This will eventually give us our user places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 133.47,
          "end": 136.293,
          "en": "or just places here, however you want to name it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 137.25,
          "end": 139.98,
          "en": "And of course that's the data which we then want use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 139.98,
          "end": 144.423,
          "en": "to set our user places like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 146.64,
          "end": 149.73,
          "en": "But, of course, fetching could also go wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 154.73,
          "en": "So just as before, we should wrap this with try catch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 154.92000000000002,
          "end": 157.98,
          "en": "And, in addition, here I also wanna manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 157.98,
          "end": 161.55,
          "en": "some loading state because initially we, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 161.55,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "won't have any places and I want to communicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 168.48,
          "en": "to the website visitor that we're currently fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 168.48,
          "end": 172.083,
          "en": "those places to provide a better user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 173.43,
          "end": 177.54,
          "en": "So therefore, just as before, in the available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 177.54,
          "end": 182.373,
          "en": "JSX file, we now should add a fetching and an error state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 183.21,
          "end": 186.18,
          "en": "And therefore I'll actually copy these states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 186.18,
          "end": 190.47,
          "en": "from available places into app JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 190.47,
          "end": 193.56,
          "en": "And I'll just get rid of this available places state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 193.56,
          "end": 195.9,
          "en": "which I don't need here but I will need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 195.9,
          "end": 199.17000000000002,
          "en": "the other two states, along with the data state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 199.17000000000002,
          "end": 202.84,
          "en": "the user places state which we set once we have the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 204.69,
          "end": 209.69,
          "en": "and now it starts with setting is fetching to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 210.93,
          "end": 213.52,
          "en": "inside of fetchPlaces when we start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 214.74,
          "end": 218.163,
          "en": "and to false after this try catch block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 219,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "And here we just need to do this once after try catch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 224.867,
          "en": "because we got no other nested code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 224.867,
          "end": 228.51,
          "en": "that would run independently as we did it before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 228.51,
          "end": 231.963,
          "en": "with AvailablePlaces and getCurrentPosition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 233.13,
          "end": 236.73,
          "en": "We don't have that here and therefore one satisfaction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 236.73,
          "end": 239.763,
          "en": "false call after try catch is enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 242.07,
          "end": 244.69,
          "en": "Now, in the catch block we should call setError",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 245.97,
          "end": 247.86,
          "en": "and set this equal to an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 247.86,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "where we have a message property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 253.05,
          "en": "which is error.message or some fallback property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 253.05,
          "end": 255.813,
          "en": "like failed to fetch user places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 258.69,
          "end": 262.83,
          "en": "Well and now we can use all those different states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 262.83,
          "end": 267.27,
          "en": "I mean the user places state is already being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 267.27,
          "end": 268.71,
          "en": "in the JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 268.71,
          "end": 271.353,
          "en": "It's passed to this places component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 272.43,
          "end": 277.38,
          "en": "But now we can also pass a loadingText and isLoading prompt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 277.38,
          "end": 280.5,
          "en": "to places just as we did it before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 280.5,
          "end": 282.783,
          "en": "in the AvailablePlaces component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 283.725,
          "end": 287.19,
          "en": "IsLoading should get the value of isFetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 287.19,
          "end": 290.4,
          "en": "so true or false depending on whether the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 290.4,
          "end": 292.40999999999997,
          "en": "is on its way or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 292.40999999999997,
          "end": 295.17,
          "en": "And loading text gets our loading message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 295.17,
          "end": 298.627,
          "en": "which could be \"Fetching your places...\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 300.84,
          "end": 304.44,
          "en": "Now if things go wrong, I also wanna show an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 304.44,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "and therefore, I'll conditionally output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 309.48,
          "en": "based on this error state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 309.48,
          "end": 313.827,
          "en": "My error component here where I set the title to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 313.827,
          "end": 318.827,
          "en": "\"An error occurred,\" and the message to my error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 321.69,
          "end": 324.603,
          "en": "or there to the error message to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 326.88,
          "end": 330.24,
          "en": "Places should only be rendered if we have no error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 330.24,
          "end": 332.7,
          "en": "So here I'll check if not error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 332.7,
          "end": 335.313,
          "en": "and in that case I'm rendering my places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 337.53,
          "end": 341.22,
          "en": "And with all that, if we now save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 341.22,
          "end": 343.22,
          "en": "now we fetch that data from the back end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 344.46,
          "end": 347.46,
          "en": "and to see that, we also see that loading message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 347.46,
          "end": 351.9,
          "en": "We can again throttle the network to slow 3G",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 351.9,
          "end": 354.42,
          "en": "and reload and wait for this page to load.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 354.42,
          "end": 358.59000000000003,
          "en": "But once the page did load, we should then actually also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 358.59000000000003,
          "end": 362.16,
          "en": "that loading text in that first box briefly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 362.16,
          "end": 364.41,
          "en": "So here we see fetching your places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 364.41,
          "end": 367.35,
          "en": "and then the place data arrives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 367.35,
          "end": 368.793,
          "en": "So that is working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 369.72,
          "end": 373.65,
          "en": "Now if things go wrong, which I will again simulate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 373.65,
          "end": 378.3,
          "en": "by adding a couple of extra Ss here to this URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 378.3,
          "end": 380.883,
          "en": "you see we got this error box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 383.04,
          "end": 385.263,
          "en": "So error handling also works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 386.37,
          "end": 388.23,
          "en": "And with that, I'll get rid of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 388.23,
          "end": 391.83,
          "en": "And this is now the finished application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 391.83,
          "end": 394.86,
          "en": "where we can load available places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 394.86,
          "end": 397.95,
          "en": "add those places and store them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 397.95,
          "end": 402.24,
          "en": "and then also reload to re-fetch those stored places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 402.24,
          "end": 405.87,
          "en": "update that if we want to or don't update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 405.87,
          "end": 409.59000000000003,
          "en": "if we don't want to and we got this all working now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 409.59000000000003,
          "end": 414.12,
          "en": "with a separate backend which is used to store that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 414.12,
          "end": 416.64,
          "en": "And the great thing about that separate backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 416.64,
          "end": 419.58,
          "en": "is that this can now be used by users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 419.58,
          "end": 421.29,
          "en": "from all over the world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 421.29,
          "end": 424.11,
          "en": "The data is no longer stored locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 424.11,
          "end": 427.62,
          "en": "in the React application and you are therefore now able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 427.62,
          "end": 431.703,
          "en": "to build more powerful and versatile React applications.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}